223
00:16:28,909 --> 00:16:30,569
You should now be able to say:

224
00:16:30,909 --> 00:16:36,034
A uses line runs someone else's code with
your job's token and secrets, and a tag in

225
00:16:36,074 --> 00:16:38,125
it is resolved again on every run.

226
00:16:38,465 --> 00:16:43,569
A tag is a movable ref; a full commit ID
names content that cannot change, and it is

227
00:16:43,609 --> 00:16:46,386
the only immutable way
to reference an action.

228
00:16:46,726 --> 00:16:51,276
A pin is the commit ID with the version
as a comment, taken from the action's own

229
00:16:51,316 --> 00:16:55,584
repository and updated by Dependabot,
with a default cooldown of three days.

230
00:16:55,924 --> 00:17:00,452
Pinning does not vouch for the pinned code,
does not cover nested unpinned actions

231
00:17:00,492 --> 00:17:03,460
or downloaded scripts, and
gives up Dependabot alerts.

232
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:08,727
Organization policies can restrict which
actions run and require pinning; reviewing

233
00:17:08,767 --> 00:17:12,138
the workflow files still needs
code owners and a ruleset.

